      "message": "\u003e I added java_import for the module starting with art-module-sdk_* (e.g. art-module-sdk_art.module.api.annotations.for.system.modules) in apex_contributions\u0027 contents. However, the visibility for this is private and therefore I can easily configured the dependency for v2. I am not sure if we really need them as part of apex contributions or we can just treat it in similar manner as license.\n\nI think you are right. These soong modules are internal to the module sdk - they are used to bootstrap other soong modules in prebuilts/module_sdk, but are not used by the rest of the build. I have updated the CL to filter them out using `builder.isInternalMember`\n\n\u003e BTW, I think art-module-sdk_art.module.api.annotations.for.system.modules is part of sdk gen and we probably don\u0027t have the source version, is that correct? I think I cannot put source_module_name like others.\n\nLooking at its usages, I think its source is `art.module.api.annotations.for.system.modules` (https://diff.googleplex.com/#key\u003dUf4xvA1RXjMk). This module does seem to be internal to the module sdk though (it will not be present in the autogenerated `apex_contributions_defaults`). I think we can skip addition of `source_module_name` property if it makes the autogeneration script more maintainable.",
